WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
Take some copper oxide,
and remove its oxygen.

2
00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.990
You're left with shiny copper metal.

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.090
Chemists call that reduction.

4
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.730
But nothing got smaller.

5
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.510
Nothing was cut down.

6
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.050
And it gets stranger.

7
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.150
Chemists also call some
reactions oxidation,

8
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.070
even when there's no
oxygen involved at all.

9
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.550
So what do these two
words really mean?

10
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.310
What are they keeping track of?

11
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.030
In this mission, you'll see
oxidation and reduction as the gain

12
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.400
and loss of oxygen.

13
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.210
You'll meet a second way to
define them, using electrons.

14
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.590
And you'll find out what oxidising
agents and reducing agents

15
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.610
do.

16
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.290
Your mission: work out what
oxidation and reduction really

17
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.390
track.
